## Casablanca, Beijing, Rotterdam

My path so far runs through three cities. I studied computer science, then moved to China to study Chinese at Nankai University. I stayed for seven years in Beijing, where I grew from web designer and developer into a UX designer leading more than 30 projects. Today I work from Rotterdam.

## Design and build, under one roof

Because I started out writing code, I still build a lot of what I design. That means fewer surprises between the mockup and the live product, and decisions made with real constraints in mind.

## Your problem becomes my problem

The best work I've done happened when I stopped acting like a supplier and started acting like part of the team. I start with users and data rather than opinions, keep the loops short, and ship early so we can learn and improve.

## Away from the screen

Music is never far away. It's what's playing while I sketch, and often what I'm listening to when an idea finally clicks.
